From: T531 Project <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] brightness: tolerate pre-GNOME-49 shortcut schemas

Phosh 0.58 aborts on Debian 13 because org.gnome.shell.keybindings from
GNOME 48 lacks the new screen brightness keys. Before GNOME 49 those
shortcuts belong to gnome-settings-daemon's media-keys schema instead.
Keep their legacy owner when running on the older schema. This does not
skip initialization of the backlight adjustment, D-Bus API or slider.

Runtime reproduction: GLib fatal error for screen-brightness-up, SIGTRAP
at startup on the SM-T531 with gnome-shell-common 48.7-0+deb13u2.

Forwarded: not-yet
---
diff --git a/src/brightness-manager.c b/src/brightness-manager.c
--- a/src/brightness-manager.c
+++ b/src/brightness-manager.c
@@ -808,6 +808,7 @@ phosh_brightness_manager_init (PhoshBrightnessManager *self)
 {
   PhoshShell *shell = phosh_shell_get_default ();
   PhoshAmbient *ambient = phosh_shell_get_ambient (phosh_shell_get_default ());
+  g_autoptr (GSettingsSchema) schema = NULL;
 
   self->saved_brightness = -1.0;
   self->icon_name = "display-brightness-symbolic";
@@ -863,6 +864,17 @@ phosh_brightness_manager_init (PhoshBrightnessManager *self)
                            self,
                            G_CONNECT_SWAPPED);
 
+  schema = g_settings_schema_source_lookup (g_settings_schema_source_get_default (),
+                                            KEYBINDINGS_SCHEMA_ID, TRUE);
+  if (!schema ||
+      !g_settings_schema_has_key (schema, KEYBINDING_KEY_BRIGHTNESS_UP) ||
+      !g_settings_schema_has_key (schema, KEYBINDING_KEY_BRIGHTNESS_DOWN) ||
+      !g_settings_schema_has_key (schema, KEYBINDING_KEY_BRIGHTNESS_UP_MONITOR) ||
+      !g_settings_schema_has_key (schema, KEYBINDING_KEY_BRIGHTNESS_DOWN_MONITOR)) {
+    g_debug ("Keeping brightness shortcuts with the legacy settings daemon");
+    return;
+  }
+
   self->settings = g_settings_new (KEYBINDINGS_SCHEMA_ID);
   g_signal_connect_object (self->settings,
                            "changed",
